MonoBehaviour:
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 075ae7a4e0c44354e9959697c9e269fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: Redundant Industry
  legacyName: Redundant Industry
  description: '+5% Production across the civilization.'
  flavorText: 'The engineers who restored the damaged industrial system returned with little patience for anything described as a ''single point of failure.'' Spare capacity was distributed between facilities, replacement parts standardized, alternate supply lines mapped, and important processes designed so that one broken machine did not silence an entire chain of production. To accountants in quiet years, redundancy sometimes looked wasteful. To anyone who remembered factories standing idle because one indispensable component had failed, it looked like survival. The result was an industrial economy that could keep producing even while pieces of it were being repaired.'
